WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.875
Unit 2 is the five closure conditions.

2
00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:06.527
The data platform book, Data
Platform: SQL Server Identity,

3
00:00:06.527 --> 00:00:10.301
defines the transformation as
complete when five conditions

4
00:00:10.301 --> 00:00:13.350
hold at the same time on
every production instance.

5
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.709
One: no usable Windows-backed principal,

6
00:00:15.709 --> 00:00:19.212
other than the break-glass
group in the exception registry.

7
00:00:19.212 --> 00:00:21.987
Two: SQL Authentication eliminated.

8
00:00:21.987 --> 00:00:26.924
No SQL logins outside the registry,
the S A account disabled and renamed,

9
00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:30.506
and SQL logins refused,
which on SQL Server 2025

10
00:00:30.506 --> 00:00:34.088
also needs is external
authentication only set to one.

11
00:00:34.088 --> 00:00:38.299
Three: Entra authentication
observed working, and nothing else:

12
00:00:38.299 --> 00:00:43.703
every usable login is an Entra type, the
sign-in logs and SQL Server Audit show it,

13
00:00:43.703 --> 00:00:47.200
and there are no remote N T
L M or Kerberos connections.

14
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:52.357
Four: a cloud identity for the engine:
the Arc agent connected, the SQL extension

15
00:00:52.357 --> 00:00:57.362
deployed, and Entra configured, which
failover cluster instances don't support.

16
00:00:57.362 --> 00:00:59.762
Five: M F A for every human.

17
00:00:59.762 --> 00:01:01.888
None of them is a single engine setting.

18
00:01:01.888 --> 00:01:05.590
Login mode one proves only
that SQL logins are refused.
